LIBPKGCHECK-EXEC(7)

# NAME

libpkgcheck-exec - native check execution adapter

# DESCRIPTION

*libpkgcheck-exec* admits concrete source, built-package, check-input, root-view,
and temporary trees for one sealed *libpkgcheck* request. It translates the
source-owned check program into a backend-neutral *libpkgexec* request with
purpose *check*, invokes one backend, and seals terminal *libpkgcheck* evidence.

Check-input trees are matched by exact input authority and retained in the
canonical order of the sealed request. Caller order is not semantically
significant. Missing, duplicate, unrelated, and tree-mismatched input authority
is rejected.

Concrete source, package, input, and temporary paths must be absolute, non-root,
and mutually disjoint after lexical normalization. Distinct admitted semantic
resources must not share one concrete resource identity. The root-view path is
a separate namespace coordinate and may be the filesystem root.

# DURABLE EVIDENCE

The versioned check-execution codec retains the exact *libpkgexec* execution
record and adapter-owned terminal outcome, failure classification, and
evidence identities. Decode requires the exact check request, execution
request, and backend profile bodies. It does not reconstruct authorities from
identity strings and performs no filesystem or execution effect.

# AUTHORITY

The library does not unpack artifacts, perform process syscalls, schedule
transaction nodes, or publish controller progression.

# SEE ALSO

*pkgcheck_exec_result_codec*(3), *libpkgcheck*(3), *libpkgexec*(3)
